course: dictionary
lesson: 5448
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. Landing is one of these words. «The first Moon landing was on 20 July 1969.» Here a landing is when a spacecraft comes down to the surface of the Moon.
explain: A landing can also be a flat place. Think of the stairs in a house: the landing is the flat bit at the top, or between two flights of stairs. To check, put your meaning into the sentence. If «Wait on the flat bit at the top of the stairs» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The verb form, landing, means coming down to the ground or arriving. «Flaps and slats slide out of the wing at take-off and landing» is about a plane. Take-off is the opposite of landing, so the words around it tell you the meaning.
fact: A landing is when an aircraft, spacecraft or bird comes down to the ground or water.
fact: A landing is the flat area at the top of stairs or between two flights of stairs.
fact: A landing can also be a place where boats stop to load and unload.
fact: «The first Moon landing was on 20 July 1969.»
fact: Flaps and slats slide out of a plane's wing at take-off and landing, so it can fly slowly without falling.
exercise: «The first Moon landing was on 20 July 1969.» What does landing mean here? | A jump over a fence | A boat stopping to load its cargo | A flat area at the top of stairs | * A spacecraft coming down to the surface of the Moon
exercise: Mum calls, «Wait on the landing, I'm coming up.» Which meaning of landing is this? | A plane coming down to the ground | * The flat area between flights of stairs | A dog barking at the door | A place where boats stop
exercise: In «at take-off and landing», what is the opposite of take-off? | Sleeping | * Landing | Stairs | Waiting
test: In «crash landing», what does landing mean? | Going up the stairs | * Coming down to the ground, badly and too hard | Swimming across a lake | Taking a rest
test: Look at «The plane is landing now.» What does landing mean in this sentence? | * Coming down to the ground | Singing | Sleeping | Taking off
exam: Which sentence uses landing to mean a flat place? | The astronauts' first landing was in 1969. | The bird made a soft landing on the branch. | * Mia waited on the landing at the top of the stairs. | The plane made a safe landing.
